@startuml
title Session key flow — two keys, two signatures
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
}

actor "Owner\n(user key)" as Owner
participant "App" as App
participant "Session key\n(local secp256k1)" as SK
participant "Wallet APIs" as API
participant "Smart account\n(MAv2)" as Acct

App -> SK : generate keypair
App -> API : wallet_createSession(account, chainId,\nexpirySec, key.publicKey, permissions[])
API --> App : sessionId + EIP-712 signatureRequest
App -> Owner : sign the session grant
Owner --> App : session signature\n(no personal_sign prefix)

note over Owner, SK #EEF5FF
  The owner signs once. Every call
  below is signed by the session key.
end note

App -> API : wallet_prepareCalls(calls,\ncapabilities.permissions = {sessionId, signature},\ncapabilities.paymasterService.policyId)
API --> App : UserOperation + hash to sign
App -> SK : sign the hash
SK --> App : userOp signature
App -> API : wallet_sendPreparedCalls(payload,\npermissions, signature)
API -> Acct : bundled as a UserOperation
Acct -> Acct : install the session key validation\n(deferred action, if not yet installed)
Acct -> Acct : run permission hooks:\nTimeRange, Allowlist, NativeTokenLimit
API --> App : call ID
@enduml
